{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic","id":294948,"title":"Wastelands no longer automatic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-28T09:51:52-07:00","id":294948,"title":"Wastelands no longer automatic","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So what causes a Wasteland? Prometheans don\u2019t cause them just by existing; the Divine Fire isn\u2019t <i>that</i> intense. But the following actions or events can start or worsen the process. Once a Wasteland has begun, the only way to reverse it to remove the Divine Fire (i.e., the Promethean) from the area.<ul><li>A single Promethean spends a great deal of Pyros in a scene. The amount required depends on the Promethean\u2019s Azoth dots. Greater Azoth burns brighter and hotter than the Pyros of a less potent Created. The amount required is (11 \u2013 Azoth). The most powerful Prometheans cause a Wasteland with even the slightest usage of Pyros.</li> <li>Prometheans can return to life when destroyed (once). This causes an enormous rush of Pyros, not dissimilar to a new Promethean\u2019s creation.</li> <li>When a greater <i>qashmal</i> manifests, a Wasteland can occur.</li> <li>When a character attempts to create a Promethean \u2014 successful or not \u2014 the coalescence of Pyros that accompanies the practice creates or exacerbates Wastelands.</li> <li>When a Promethean attains a universal milestone, the influx of Pyros can cause Wasteland.</li> <li>If a Promethean goes too long without a Refinement shift, or without a milestone, the buildup of excess Pyros can taint the area around her. At lower levels of Azoth (1-2), this occurs after six months in an area. At mid levels (3-5), this occurs after a single month. At higher levels (6-7), only a week must pass. The greatest Created (8-10) must evolve quickly \u2014 indeed, daily \u2014 move along, or cause a Wasteland.</li> <li>When Pandorans awake, they can shake an area into a Wasteland. When Pandorans whose Ranks total 4 or more awaken in a single scene, they create a Wasteland.</li> <li>Any suitably dramatic event culminating in a massive influx of Pyros can spawn or grow a Wasteland, at Storyteller discretion.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>So Wastelands are no longer automatic. They just show up if we use out powers, or come back to life, or create a new Promethean. Or if our enemies show up. Or if our allies show up. Or if we progress on the Pilgrimage. Or if we don't progress on the Pilgrimage. Also, sometimes for no reason at all.<br /> <br /> Paddlin' the school canoe? That's a Wasteland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T10:09:41-07:00","id":294972,"title":"","content":"Just so people who don't follow the blogs can play along:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/disquiet-and-the-wasteland-everything-and-everyone-hates-you/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/disquiet-and-...one-hates-you/</a><br /> <br /> Spoilers about disquiet and wasteland! And a stealth spoiler about Universal Milestones. That being said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic#post294948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Paddlin' the school canoe? That's a Wasteland.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite follow what you mean by this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T10:14:10-07:00","id":294975,"title":"","content":"I think that the intention behind this change is that now characters can live and have a long downtime without them simply being crushed under &quot;WE NEED TO MOVE!&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's nice because now the players will think twice before using pyros-powered abilities. Remember that in first edition, most 1-dot powers were completelly free. But now, using powers come with the thought that you might scorch the land you try to call home, and doing so will break your efforts. So when some baddy comes around and goes all-out on you, you might choose to simply punch him dead rather than thunderbolting his face until it's melted.<br /> <br /> And, you know, Wasteland now becomes a dramatic effect rather than bean-counting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T13:07:36-07:00","id":295115,"title":"","content":"&quot;Paddlin' the school canoe&quot; is a Simpsons quote, and apropo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T13:35:11-07:00","id":295150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic#post294948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Wastelands are no longer automatic. They just show up if we use out powers, or come back to life, or create a new Promethean. Or if our enemies show up. Or if our allies show up. Or if we progress on the Pilgrimage. Or if we don't progress on the Pilgrimage. Also, sometimes for no reason at all.<br /> <br /> Paddlin' the school canoe? That's a Wasteland.</div> </div> </div> </div>They haven't said that using that using your powers creates a wasteland. It does'nt even say azoth if that's what you're thinking. It says an amount of pyros based on 11 - your azoth. It doesn't even say how much pyros you have to expend. you're misrepresenting the passage you're posting here. can't you pay attention to the context of how wastelands form? besides which some promethean powers don't even use pyros to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":885,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","user":"bwgustaf","date":". 10-28-2014, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T20:07:31-07:00","id":295563,"title":"","content":"I'm glad it's not automatic, because that made the game unplayable to me. Now if only it would apply to people in the same about way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T00:01:54-07:00","id":295660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic?p=295150#post295150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They haven't said that using that using your powers creates a wasteland. It does'nt even say azoth if that's what you're thinking. It says an amount of pyros based on 11 - your azoth. It doesn't even say how much pyros you have to expend. you're misrepresenting the passage you're posting here. can't you pay attention to the context of how wastelands form? besides which some promethean powers don't even use pyros to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that he's provided the text in the exact same post, you can't call what he said a misrepresentation. It's just a quick, tongue-in-cheek summary of what he's already said. Be fair, dude, and don't drown the thread in pedantry, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T01:37:00-07:00","id":295673,"title":"","content":"For symmetric and logical reasons I would only apply the &quot;no Refinement shift&quot; condition to work after six months for Azoth 1-3 characters and one month for Azoth 4-5 characters. It's because, from mine observation, &quot;typical&quot; monster character in nWoD ends at about Power Stat 3 - in <b>Vampire</b> you are &quot;mature&quot; Kindred, but not real Elder. In <b>Werewolf</b> you are &quot;true hunter&quot;, but there are those higher than you. In <b>Mage</b> you entered Legacy and you mostly settled in power for your life. Most NPCs end they development at Power Stat 3 - only PCs or not ordinary character goes higher. Beside, it will makes nicer pyramid write-up - first 3 levels for 6 months, then 2 levels for one month, then 2 levels for two weeks, 2 level for one week and 1 final level for everyday change. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T04:26:23-07:00","id":295704,"title":"","content":"Do we know what &quot;Refinement Shift&quot; means anyway? Refinements haven't been spoiled yet.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean, it could mean &quot;change Refinement&quot; as much as &quot;change Role within the same Refinement&quot; or maybe other things entirely. Isn't a bit too early to try to fix something wich we don't know how works?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-29-2014, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T05:27:32-07:00","id":295729,"title":"","content":"What if the Integrity trait was about how closely you followed your Refinement? Hitting 0 means Centimanni, breaking points are Refinemnt shifts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T07:23:05-07:00","id":295837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic?p=295563#post295563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad it's not automatic, because that made the game unplayable to me. Now if only it would apply to people in the same about way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that it does. Disquiet doesn't get people to mob you until you Wasteland, right? That's how I read this paragraph:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Disquiet, by itself, doesn\u2019t progress beyond a certain point. People feel suspicious, fascinated, or just disdainful with regards to the Promethean, and might go out of their way to cause minor inconveniences, but it doesn\u2019t rise to the level of physical violence. Within a Wasteland, though, Disquiet festers. The human mind responds not only to the intensity of the Divine Fire within the Promethean, but to the changes she is wreaking on the environment. Left unchecked, Disquiet becomes contagious, and ends with the victims trying to purge the corrosive element from their midst (this is colloquially known as the \u201ctorches and pitchforks\u201d stage of Disquiet).</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T10:45:40-07:00","id":296002,"title":"","content":"That's how I read it at least. Unless there's a Wasteland, commoners don't start getting the torches and pitchforks (and even then, the Wasteland just seems to enable those kind of Disquiet levels, not prompt them, but I'm not sure about that part). There's still plenty of bad things about Disquiet before that stage so avoiding it to grow is always desireable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T00:30:39-07:00","id":296723,"title":"","content":"This does make the game much more enjoyable. I wonder if, because they now have a better chance of carving out a small notch for themselves, that some sort of small &quot;culture&quot; can exist among Prometheans now that a few could have the option of being stationary. If a Created can exist in a are for awhile, and that they are numerous enough for entire alchemist societies exist to hunt them down, that this means that Prometheans have created &quot;cultural customs&quot; amongst themselves at this point beyond etched pilgrim marks or rambles when they meet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T06:27:44-07:00","id":297051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic?p=296002#post296002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's how I read it at least. Unless there's a Wasteland, commoners don't start getting the torches and pitchforks (and even then, the Wasteland just seems to enable those kind of Disquiet levels, not prompt them, but I'm not sure about that part). There's still plenty of bad things about Disquiet before that stage so avoiding it to grow is always desireable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little confused by the new metaphysics, I think.<br /> <br /> OK, so Disquiet used to be an &quot;uncanny valley&quot; effect rubbing people the wrong way, caused by the Promethean seeming off/wrong. Now it's metaphorical &quot;Azoth radiation poisoning&quot;.<br /> <br /> Wastelands ... were pretty much always &quot;Azoth radiation poisoning&quot; - so that hasn't changed - with a sprinkling of animals and such having similar unpredictable reactions to something unnatural.<br /> <br /> But now they include part of what used to be Disquiet, mechanically - I think. It's not just that at high Wasteland levels people start going crazy sometimes, Wasteland now includes &quot;torches and pitchforks&quot; and Golems being treated like uncooperative servants by people.<br /> <br /> So ... where did the &quot;unnatural&quot; aspect go?<br /> <br /> I can see why it might cause, for example, the human element of an Unfleshed Wasteland - a small town society being disrupted by this person who behaves like a machine. There's a ton of stories about robots and clones causing a commodification of personhood, similar to e.g. slavery.<br /> <br /> But <i>now</i> it's caused by the Divine Fire damaging the environment, messing with oil. Just like Osiran Wastelands result in soured water sources.<br /> <br /> ... how? How do intense sources of the Divine Fire (like Quasmallim, even!) cause humans to behave <i>as if</i> they were encountering such an out-of-order thing and reacting to it? Shouldn't it just result in all the cars in the area spontaneously breaking down?<br /> <br /> (Still, finally Wasteland and Disquiet mechanics are unified. That was always awkward. It looks like they'll be really good!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 10-30-2014, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T08:39:58-07:00","id":297150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic?p=297051#post297051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so Disquiet used to be an &quot;uncanny valley&quot; effect rubbing people the wrong way, caused by the Promethean seeming off/wrong. Now it's metaphorical &quot;Azoth radiation poisoning&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The latter goes back to 1e core and the former is fanon that isn't supported by the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T09:13:19-07:00","id":297175,"title":"","content":"I like the wasteland change, but I am not sure if I quite fancy the seemingly softening up, of Disquiet. If Disquiet has been made too soft, it might damage or outright slay one of the core themes of Promethean - that it fundamentally sucks being a Promethean.<br /> I'm not going to stand around pointing fingers and screaming like an idiot, before the book is out and I've had a chance to read it, but it looks like they're going in a direction I cant quite agree with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T09:28:41-07:00","id":297180,"title":"","content":"I'm viewing it now that Disquiet is caused by a Promethean's lack of a soul and fundamentally un-human nature; you are a corpse held together with stitches and powered by magic, which humans and animals can subconsciously pick up on and are made uncomfortable by. By contrast, Wastelands are the result of blatant Pyros leakage (primarily through Transmutations or attempted generative acts), which has a much more severe effect of breaking down the environment and overtly impacting human actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T09:41:09-07:00","id":297188,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why you would, when Matt made it clear what's going on, but sure, run with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T16:19:49-07:00","id":297582,"title":"","content":"I still like the idea that Prometheans are fundamentally wrong rather than SO AWESOME THIS UNIVERSE CAN'T EVEN.<br /> <br /> But...when I say it like that, I can understand the change","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T17:06:35-07:00","id":297606,"title":"","content":"THere is something fundamentally wrong with them.<br /> <br /> Something that is only supposed to be here in flashes is instead <i>constantly</i> <i>going on at all times, lashing the world with undirected change, which manifests as entropy</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T08:51:20-07:00","id":298184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic?p=297606#post297606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THere is something fundamentally wrong with them.<br /> <br /> Something that is only supposed to be here in flashes is instead <i>constantly</i> <i>going on at all times, lashing the world with undirected change, which manifests as entropy</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hey, it clicked for me finally. It's not so much that I disliked it before or after the blog, just that I never really understood the why. That analogy was a good one. Have an Internet point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T10:27:05-07:00","id":298279,"title":"","content":"Arcane Arts, force of Clarity.<br /> <br /> ...wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T20:31:05-08:00","id":300689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic?p=294975#post294975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the intention behind this change is that now characters can live and have a long downtime without them simply being crushed under &quot;WE NEED TO MOVE!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure we have moved away from that in effect though. It's now no longer time based, but several of these things are inevitabilities within an active game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T22:26:27-08:00","id":300759,"title":"","content":"Of course they're inevitable. This is as it should be. Disquiet and Wastelands are the overwhelming pressure that makes the Saturnine Night unbearable. They should not be vulnerable to being gamed out as threats.<br /> <br /> The problem for me was that the system left it up to the dice rather than story needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T02:04:37-08:00","id":300902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic?p=300759#post300759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disquiet and Wastelands are the overwhelming pressure that makes the Saturnine Night unbearable. They should not be vulnerable to being gamed out as threats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, now. I could see it in a character focused on said &quot;gaming out&quot;. Like an Ordo Dracul vampire can &quot;game out&quot; the usual vampiric Banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T10:44:00-08:00","id":301298,"title":"","content":"As I mentioned in the blog comments, the key difference is that now the reins of this struggle are within the player's hands. It's a bucking bronco, to be sure, but rather than having no choice, they can at least wrestle with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T20:37:12-08:00","id":301730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic?p=300902#post300902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now. I could see it in a character focused on said &quot;gaming out&quot;. Like an Ordo Dracul vampire can &quot;game out&quot; the usual vampiric Banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I can't say I've ever particularly liked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned in the blog comments, the key difference is that now the reins of this struggle are within the player's hands. It's a bucking bronco, to be sure, but rather than having no choice, they can at least wrestle with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This however, does bear some merit to it. Games should be about choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T14:55:35-08:00","id":302709,"title":"","content":"It sounds like extra ST tracking, but could well be worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T00:45:48-08:00","id":303081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic?p=302709#post302709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like extra ST tracking, but could well be worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You only tracks how long character didn't change Refinement, or are they spending too much Pyros at once. It's not <b>that</b> complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T09:17:00-08:00","id":304666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic?p=302709#post302709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like extra ST tracking, but could well be worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Much less ST math than before, believe me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:52:10-08:00","id":304813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/294948-wastelands-no-longer-automatic?p=304666#post304666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much less ST math than before, believe me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay! I actually <i>liked</i> Disquet and Wasteland, but the latter was always too annoying to keep track of","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T16:17:47-08:00","id":305086,"title":"","content":"The new rule on Wasteland isn't all the maths all the time, and I must say that I adore how it seems to scale rather than just be 'one-size-fits-all' nonsense. THAT was one of my biggest hopes and dreams for <b>Promethean: the Created</b> Second Edition!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:47:43-08:00","id":308352,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of on the fence about the thematic change. I think it's an interesting concept that Disquiet and Wastelands are not caused by the Promethean's &quot;not meant to be&quot; status, but by the fact that so much Divine Fire in one package is too much for the world to comfortably bear. But I felt it really highlighted the theme of. . . well, being not meant to be. The whole point of Promethean is that being a Promethean is BAD, being a human is GOOD, and the underlying fact that Prometheans are unnatural aberrations that shouldn't exist was, to me, central to the premise. Changing that idea, I worry, might make the Promethean condition seem less inherently awful.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I do think an excellent point is raised in the question of &quot;if something is really not meant to exist, how can it exist?&quot; and rejecting the idea that Prometheans are inherently &quot;wrong,&quot; but still don't fit or have a place in the world. Depending on how that theme is handled, it may be a very positive change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T14:27:50-08:00","id":308517,"title":"","content":"There's something to be said for <i>incompleteness</i> as a theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakeni